flinstall -- the FreeLFS installer ("FreeLFS install")
=====================================================

Two programs, C17, MIT.

  flinstall          (/usr/bin) the window, on libflui. Steps: Language, Keyboard, Wi-Fi,
                     Disk, Account, Time zone, Summary, Install (progress, then Restart).
                     It never touches a disk.
  flinstall-helper   (/usr/libexec) the privileged half. Installed setuid root for the group
                     seat (recipe owner= "... 0 98 4750", like flpower and fltime-set).

The start menu entry (flinstall.desktop, System) has TryExec=/run/live, a directory only the
live system has (flinitrd), so an installed system does not show it. Nothing else is live
specific in the window; the helper checks for itself.

The steps
  Language    12 languages; sets LANG for programs through /etc/profile.d/20-lang.sh (a text
              console keeps C.UTF-8). It suggests a keyboard and a time zone. FreeLFS itself
              stays English.
  Keyboard    the four libflui layouts with the key preview and a field to try them. Written
              to /etc/keyboard.conf on the new system: the first boot (flsetup) then does not
              ask, so that step is "moved here" for installed systems; the live system still
              asks at its own first boot.
  Wi-Fi       flsettings' wifi.c (iwd over D-Bus), copied at build time. Known networks
              (/var/lib/iwd/*.psk, *.open, *.8021x) are copied to the new system. Can be skipped.
  Disk        pick a disk (the live medium, disks with something mounted and read-only disks
              are shown but cannot be chosen), then
                Use the whole disk   (default) new GPT: ESP 512 MiB + btrfs for the rest
                Install next to existing partitions   only free space: the largest gap
                             holding at least 6.5 GiB gets ESP + btrfs; GPT disks only; no
                             existing partition is touched (sfdisk --append). A blank disk
                             is treated like the whole disk.
                Manual       the partition editor: list and bar of the disk, make a partition
                             in a free gap (System, Boot, Swap, Data; size), delete, "use as"
                             (/ , /boot, swap, /drives/NAME), format (kept or erased),
                             new GPT. One disk at a time. / is always btrfs with the layout,
                             /boot is FAT32 (an existing one may be kept), data is ext4 or
                             btrfs (or kept).
  Account     full name, user name, password twice. Names are refused if they are already a user, a group
              or a folder in /home of the system, or not [a-z_][a-z0-9_-]{0,31}. The password needs 4 characters; the
              window draws it as squares and wipes it after sending it; root gets the same
              password. The user is in users (primary) and seat, audio, video, render,
              wheel, netdev.
  Time zone   the world map and search of libflui (A10), default from the language.
  Summary     the helper's own list of what will happen (a "check"), erasing in red, and for
              erasing a box to tick before the button says "Erase and install".
  Install     five steps, a progress bar for the copy, the last lines of what the helper runs.

What the helper does (everything is checked again there)
  Real mode needs euid 0, the live system (/run/live/rom is a squashfs and / an overlay) and a
  disk that /sys lists, that is not the live medium, not read-only, nothing mounted. The window
  never names a path: it sends the device it got from the helper's list.
  1  sfdisk: --append / --delete, or a new GPT; the new partitions get random PARTUUIDs, the
     helper finds their nodes by PARTUUID afterwards.
  2  wipefs and mkfs.fat / mkswap / mkfs.ext4 / mkfs.btrfs for the extra partitions.
  3  in a private mount namespace: tmpfs stage dir, an overlay of the live squashfs
     (/run/live/rom) with the changes below, @home holding only the new home (/home of the live system is left out of @), then one `mkfs.btrfs --rootdir --subvol default:@ --subvol @home --subvol @snapshots`
     (as build/50-image.sh does): no mounting of the new disk, no per-file copying.
     Progress is the helper's read count over the size of the source.
     The changes: fstab (file systems by UUID/PARTUUID, three btrfs lines, ESP, swap, data),
     keyboard.conf, profile.d/20-lang.sh, timezone + localtime, flpkg.conf snapshots = 5
     again, the live notes taken out of /etc/issue, the live user "tester" removed from
     passwd/shadow/group/gshadow, the new user added (sha512 crypt), root's hash, /home/NAME
     from /etc/skel owned by the new uid.
  4  the ESP: flboot.conf (root=PARTUUID=...) written first, `flboot-install --esp DIR` into a
     staging directory, the kernel next to it, then mcopy (mtools) writes it into the
     partition: no mount. The kernel comes from /run/live/iso/live/vmlinuz-* (build/53-iso.sh
     puts it there; the squashfs has no /boot), else /boot.
  5  sync.
  The helper uses its own tools from PATH=/usr/sbin:/usr/bin:/sbin:/bin: sfdisk wipefs
  mkfs.btrfs mkfs.fat mkfs.ext4 mkswap mcopy flboot-install (sgdisk is not in FreeLFS: sfdisk
  does the same), and refuses to start an install if one is missing, before writing anything.

The protocol (stdin/stdout, one line each, fields separated by TAB)
  window -> helper   disks | set KEY VALUE (mode whole|free|manual, disk, user, fullname,
                     password, lang, keyboard, tz) | part reset|newtable|delete DEV|
                     create START SIZE esp|root|swap|data (bytes) | format ID FS LABEL |
                     mount ID MOUNTPOINT | check | install | quit
                     New partitions are called new1, new2 ... in the order of the create lines.
  helper -> window   HELLO MODE, DISK/PART/FREE ... END, OK, ERR text, PLAN lines + OK for a
                     check, then for install STEP n total text, PROGRESS pct, CMD text (a
                     command run or, in a dry run, that would be run), LOG text, DONE | FAIL.

--dry-run   questions run (sfdisk -d, blkid -p, /sys, /proc: read only); everything that would
            write, format, mount or copy is printed as CMD lines and not done.

Test hooks (refused when the helper runs with more privilege than its caller, i.e. setuid)
  --image FILE        a regular file instead of a disk (never a device; checked with stat)
  --source DIR        the live tree to copy (default /run/live/rom)
  --kernel FILE  --iwd DIR  --workdir DIR
  FLINSTALL_FAKE=DIR  fake disks for a dry run: disks.txt (name, bytes, removable, model,
                      flags live|ro), NAME.dump (sfdisk -d output), NAME.fs
  In image mode the helper partitions the file, formats scratch files and dd's them in at
  the partition offsets (a file has no partition nodes), and runs the stage in a user and
  mount namespace, so no privilege is needed.
Window: FLINSTALL_HELPER="cmd args" replaces the helper, FLINSTALL_RESTART replaces
`flpower restart`; with FLUI_PPM: FLINSTALL_STEP=0..7 and FLINSTALL_TEST=disk=N,mode=N,
user=,full=,pw=,pw2=,lang=,kbd=,zone=,edit,edops=...,sel=,running=PCT,done,failed,confirm,
nodry (see apply_test in flinstall.c).

Tests
  tests/image-test.sh SCRATCH   the helper for real on sparse files in SCRATCH (needs a root
                                with the tools: FLFS_IMAGE_ROOT); reads the result back with
                                btrfs restore and mtools. Never names a device.
  tests/install.py              the window clicked through in headless flcomp, dry-run helper
                                on tests/fixture; checks what the helper was sent.

Not covered by any test here (needs root and a disk): the real-disk path, the setuid helper,
booting what it made, the kernel re-reading the partition table, the restart.
Not supported (decided): dual boot with Windows, other boot loaders, BIOS boot, encryption,
LVM/RAID, an own swap file.

The root account: FI_ROOT_SAME_PASSWORD in common.h is the one-line switch. 1 (now): root gets the first
user's password; 0: root is locked (shadow field "!"); the window's note follows.
